WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.919
Here's what Microsoft gives you,

2
00:00:01.919 --> 00:00:04.938
and its order of preference
is one the matrix keeps.

3
00:00:04.938 --> 00:00:08.972
On premises, a group managed
service account whenever possible,

4
00:00:08.972 --> 00:00:11.788
and a plain user account
only as a last resort.

5
00:00:11.788 --> 00:00:16.757
In the cloud, a managed identity if the
service runs in Azure and supports one,

6
00:00:16.757 --> 00:00:20.150
a service principal otherwise,
never a user account.

7
00:00:20.150 --> 00:00:24.930
Windows Server adds the delegated managed
service account, which has real limits:

8
00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:29.500
you can't move a managed service account
onto one, and delegation stops working.

9
00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:33.100
Learn turns this into two
decision tables, but no code.

10
00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:36.161
So the repository pins
the pages unmodified,

11
00:00:36.161 --> 00:00:40.510
and a small harness evaluates
each table exactly as published.
